# ============================================================================
# PengyOS Server - BusyBox configuration fragment
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stacked on board/core/busybox.fragment (layers/server.config lists both:
# BR2_PACKAGE_BUSYBOX_CONFIG_FRAGMENT_FILES is a single list, so a later layer
# replaces it rather than appending - see configs/layers/README.md).
#
# The Server toolset replaces the last BusyBox applets an agent would meet on a
# remote node: the network inspection tools and the cut-down PCI/USB/ATA
# readers. Each one is compiled out here and provided by the package named in
# layers/server.config.
# ============================================================================

# --- net-tools / iputils / traceroute own the network tools -----------------
# BusyBox's netstat has no -tulpn service column, its ping has no -W, its
# traceroute has no -n -m -q, and `ifconfig`/`route` are there at all only
# because iproute2's `ip` is the real interface.
# CONFIG_NETSTAT is not set
# CONFIG_IFCONFIG is not set
# CONFIG_IFUP is not set
# CONFIG_IFDOWN is not set
# CONFIG_ROUTE is not set
# CONFIG_ARP is not set
# CONFIG_ARPING is not set
# CONFIG_PING is not set
# CONFIG_TRACEROUTE is not set
# CONFIG_IPADDR is not set
# CONFIG_IPLINK is not set
# CONFIG_IPROUTE is not set
# CONFIG_IPRULE is not set
# CONFIG_IPNEIGH is not set
# CONFIG_IPTUNNEL is not set

# --- pciutils / usbutils / hdparm own the hardware readers ------------------
# BusyBox's lspci/lsusb print numbers, not names (no pci.ids/usb.ids), and its
# hdparm has no -I (the drive-identity dump an agent uses to size a disk).
# CONFIG_LSPCI is not set
# CONFIG_LSUSB is not set
# CONFIG_HDPARM is not set
